WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.534 --> 00:00:19.269
On Saturday morning, Joy sat at the kitchen table working on her report.

2
00:00:19.270 --> 00:00:24.719
She had been reading an article on the Internet called "Being a Friend."

3
00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:29.319
But now she closed Mom's laptop and sat thinking.

4
00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:32.117
"What's on your mind?" asked Grandpa.

5
00:00:32.118 --> 00:00:35.193
Joy looked up and grinned.

6
00:00:35.194 --> 00:00:38.462
"I've got a great idea," she said.

7
00:00:38.463 --> 00:00:39.992
"I'll be right back!"

8
00:00:39.993 --> 00:00:42.563
Joy ran out of the kitchen.

9
00:00:42.564 --> 00:00:47.130
When she returned, her arms were loaded with art supplies.

10
00:00:47.131 --> 00:00:52.504
"Whew!" she said, dumping everything on the kitchen table.

11
00:00:52.505 --> 00:00:55.833
"What are you going to make?" asked Grandpa.

12
00:00:55.834 --> 00:00:59.861
He stirred the pot on the stove with a big spoon.

13
00:00:59.862 --> 00:01:04.980
"My own special invention!" Joy laughed.

14
00:01:04.981 --> 00:01:07.983
First, she cut a paddle from cardboard.

15
00:01:07.984 --> 00:01:12.022
Then, she cut a pointer from black paper.

16
00:01:12.023 --> 00:01:16.679
She fastened the pointer to the cardboard and gave it a spin.

17
00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:19.176
"Perfect!" she said.

18
00:01:19.177 --> 00:01:23.396
Grandpa sipped a mouthful of soup from the pot.

19
00:01:23.397 --> 00:01:27.524
"With a little salt, this chicken soup should be perfect too.

20
00:01:27.525 --> 00:01:31.445
I wonder if Katie will make it home in time for lunch."

21
00:01:31.446 --> 00:01:38.936
Joy drew two big dots on the cardboard, one with a green marker and one with a red marker.

22
00:01:38.937 --> 00:01:45.790
Then she drew a smiley face on the green dot and a frowning face on the red dot.

23
00:01:45.791 --> 00:01:50.632
She drew blue zigzags along the edges of the cardboard.

24
00:01:50.633 --> 00:01:54.919
She held up her work to admire it. "It's done!"

25
00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:57.707
"And so is lunch!" Grandpa said.

26
00:01:57.708 --> 00:02:01.501
He placed a bowl of soup for Joy on the table.

27
00:02:01.502 --> 00:02:05.313
He looked at her invention and scratched his head.

28
00:02:05.314 --> 00:02:09.942
"It looks good, but . . . what is it?"

29
00:02:09.943 --> 00:02:13.253
"It's a friendship meter!" said Joy.

30
00:02:13.254 --> 00:02:17.499
With her thumb, she moved the pointer to the green dot.

31
00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:24.060
"And it's smiling—because you, Grandpa, are the best friend a person could have!"

32
00:02:24.061 --> 00:02:27.222
Then Joy looked at the clock.

33
00:02:27.223 --> 00:02:30.144
"I better clean up," she said.

34
00:02:30.145 --> 00:02:35.205
"It's almost one o'clock—almost time for square-dance practice!"

35
00:02:35.206 --> 00:02:39.866
Katie was working on her report at the Willow Creek library.

36
00:02:39.867 --> 00:02:46.391
She had found a book called Bend and Stretch and another called Fitness for Fun.

37
00:02:46.392 --> 00:02:51.185
"Muscles are very interesting, Mr. Dexter," Katie said.

38
00:02:51.186 --> 00:02:54.749
Mr. Dexter was the Saturday librarian.

39
00:02:54.750 --> 00:02:59.390
"Did you know there is a special muscle for sticking out your tongue?"

40
00:02:59.391 --> 00:03:02.959
Katie stuck out her tongue for Mr. Dexter.

41
00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:08.722
Mr. Dexter looked at Katie over the top of his glasses.

42
00:03:08.723 --> 00:03:12.715
"That is interesting," said Mr. Dexter.

43
00:03:12.716 --> 00:03:17.233
He continued searching through the library's music CDs.

44
00:03:17.234 --> 00:03:19.880
"Here it is!" he finally said.

45
00:03:19.881 --> 00:03:24.041
"Square-Dance Music with Easy-to-Follow Guide."

46
00:03:24.042 --> 00:03:26.666
"Perfect!" said Katie.

47
00:03:26.667 --> 00:03:29.318
She opened the CD case.

48
00:03:29.319 --> 00:03:35.599
She unfolded a paper that showed couples doing square-dance steps. "I'll take it!"

49
00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:39.891
Katie loaded everything into her backpack and peeked at her watch.

50
00:03:39.892 --> 00:03:42.057
It was time to go!

51
00:03:42.058 --> 00:03:47.315
"Thank you for your help, Mr. Dexter," she said and spun around.

52
00:03:47.316 --> 00:03:50.378
There stood Olivia Sprinkle.

53
00:03:50.379 --> 00:03:54.264
"Aloha! Hello!" said Olivia.

54
00:03:54.265 --> 00:03:57.990
"Aloha, good-bye," said Katie.

55
00:03:57.991 --> 00:04:01.663
"Who is this?" said Mr. Dexter.

56
00:04:01.664 --> 00:04:07.358
"Olivia Sprinkle," said Katie. "She's in the fourth grade too."

57
00:04:07.359 --> 00:04:11.677
Just then the phone on Mr. Dexter's desk rang.

58
00:04:11.678 --> 00:04:13.750
"Excuse me," he said.

59
00:04:13.751 --> 00:04:17.355
"Katie, please show Olivia around the library."

60
00:04:17.356 --> 00:04:22.084
"But—" said Katie. "I have to go home. My—"

61
00:04:22.085 --> 00:04:24.526
Mr. Dexter wasn't listening.

62
00:04:24.527 --> 00:04:27.751
He was already busy on the phone.

63
00:04:27.752 --> 00:04:31.275
"That would be great, Katie!" said Olivia.

64
00:04:31.276 --> 00:04:34.663
"Maybe you can help me with my skin report."

65
00:04:34.664 --> 00:04:39.309
"It sounds like Miss Smarty-Pants needs help," Katie thought.

66
00:04:39.310 --> 00:04:44.929
"I know about keeping skin clean and protecting it from the sun," said Olivia.

67
00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:48.429
"But that's not enough for a whole report."

68
00:04:48.430 --> 00:04:51.104
Katie raised her eyebrows.

69
00:04:51.105 --> 00:04:56.664
"Aren't you going to talk about poison ivy or ticks?" she asked.

70
00:04:56.665 --> 00:05:00.705
"Ticks? What's that?" asked Olivia.

71
00:05:00.706 --> 00:05:04.464
Katie loved telling people about ticks.

72
00:05:04.465 --> 00:05:08.782
"You really do need help," she said, sighing.

73
00:05:08.783 --> 00:05:13.710
"Maybe we should sit down."
